# STR Operations Case Study – Old Town Apartments

## Overview
This case study summarizes 10+ years of operational experience managing short‑term rental units in Dubrovnik’s Old Town area. It highlights guest communication, operational workflows, issue resolution, and review performance.

## Key Metrics
- 200+ guest reviews  
- ~99% 5‑star rating  
- High accuracy in check‑in coordination  
- Strong guest satisfaction with communication and support  
- Zero no‑show cleaning incidents  
- Consistent seasonal occupancy

## Operational Strengths
### 1. Guest Communication
- Fast response times (5–10 minutes)
- Clear, structured messaging
- Multilingual support (EN/HR/ES)
- Pre‑arrival, mid‑stay, and check‑out workflows

### 2. Check‑In & Check‑Out Management
- Detailed instructions with photos
- Real‑time availability during arrival window
- Smooth coordination with cleaning teams

### 3. Issue Resolution
- Immediate acknowledgment
- Diagnosis → workaround → team coordination
- Follow‑up after resolution
- Logged incidents for pattern tracking

### 4. Listing Quality & Expectation Management
- Accurate descriptions
- Updated photos
- Clear house rules
- Seasonal pricing logic

## Guest Feedback Themes
- Excellent communication  
- Smooth check‑in  
- Cleanliness and preparation  
- Local recommendations  
- Professional support  

## Conclusion
This case study demonstrates long‑term consistency, operational reliability, and strong guest satisfaction — key indicators of a mature STR operations profile.
